sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    title HackMatch — US-019: Invitation Response — Transaction Sequence
    actor Invitee
    participant ReactUI
    participant ExpressAPI
    participant ResponseService as Response<br/>Service
    participant PostgreSQL

    Invitee->>ReactUI: Open My Invitations
    ReactUI->>ExpressAPI: GET /api/invitations/mine
    ExpressAPI->>ExpressAPI: Verify Firebase token, MFA, active verified PART
    ExpressAPI->>ResponseService: List invitations for authenticated participant
    ResponseService->>PostgreSQL: Query addressed invitations and permitted team/slot fields
    PostgreSQL-->>ResponseService: Status, expiry, team name, and vacancy role
    ResponseService-->>ReactUI: Invitation list and respondable state
    ReactUI-->>Invitee: Show Pending, final, empty, or error state

    Invitee->>ReactUI: Choose Accept or Decline
    ReactUI->>ExpressAPI: POST /api/invitations/:id/respond with decision only
    ExpressAPI->>ExpressAPI: Validate invitation id and decision without eventId
    alt Unauthorized, wrong invitee, invalid, or expired
        ExpressAPI-->>ReactUI: 400, 401, 403, or 409 with explicit code
        ReactUI-->>Invitee: Preserve list, selection, and current outcome
    else Accept
        ExpressAPI->>ResponseService: acceptInvitation for authenticated invitee
        ResponseService->>PostgreSQL: accept_team_invitation RPC
        PostgreSQL->>PostgreSQL: Serialize participant/shadow-event and target team
        PostgreSQL->>PostgreSQL: Lock and recheck Pending request, account, team, vacancy, and capacity
        PostgreSQL->>PostgreSQL: Legacy shadow-event lifecycle and event-membership checks
        PostgreSQL->>PostgreSQL: Confirm membership, fill vacancy, mark Accepted, and clear LFT rows
        PostgreSQL->>PostgreSQL: Cancel filled-slot and full-team Pending requests and persist owner alert
        alt Another transaction wins or a guard changed
            PostgreSQL-->>ResponseService: Domain or concurrency conflict
            ResponseService-->>ExpressAPI: Explicit 409 conflict
            ExpressAPI-->>ReactUI: Winning status and refresh guidance
            ReactUI-->>Invitee: Close stale actions and keep context
        else Transaction commits
            PostgreSQL-->>ResponseService: Membership, vacancy, counts, and cascade summary
            ResponseService-->>ExpressAPI: Accepted placement result
            ExpressAPI-->>ReactUI: 200 membership confirmed
            ReactUI-->>Invitee: Show roster status and cleanup notice
        end
    else Decline
        ExpressAPI->>ResponseService: declineTeamInvitation for authenticated invitee
        ResponseService->>PostgreSQL: Lock invitation and recheck Pending plus expiry
        PostgreSQL->>PostgreSQL: Mark Declined and persist invitee/owner alerts
        PostgreSQL-->>ResponseService: Declined with unchanged membership, vacancy, and LFT
        ResponseService-->>ExpressAPI: Changed or idempotent repeat result
        ExpressAPI-->>ReactUI: 200 final outcome
        ReactUI-->>Invitee: Show decline and owner-notified status
    end

    Note over PostgreSQL: The acceptance writes and cleanup commit in one transaction. Current SQL still derives locks, membership exclusion, maximum size, and part of cleanup from the Internal Shadow Event.
    Note over ReactUI,ExpressAPI: No eventId is accepted from the user, but response DTOs still expose eventId and internal participant and membership identifiers.

